@startuml
title As-Needed Checks, Local Reminder and Caregiver Delivery
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Malgun Gothic
skinparam maxMessageSize 110
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Patient
actor Caregiver
boundary "AsNeededScheduleSection /\ncaregiver settings" as UI
control "MedicationHistoryControl /\nAsNeededCheckReminderControl" as Front
boundary "Authenticated care / settings API" as API
control "ManageMedicationCare /\nSetCaregiverNotification" as Care
database "Reports + Audit + Receipt\nCaregiver outbox + Preferences" as DB
control "ProcessCaregiverAlertOutbox /\nDispatchCaregiverAlert" as Delivery
participant "FCM / caregiver client" as Push
participant "Patient NotificationService" as Local

== Independent caregiver subscription ==
Caregiver -> UI: PRN bell in linked patient's read-only schedule
UI -> API: Set as_needed preference: Off / dose_completed
API -> Care: Verify active link and caregiver scope
Care -> DB: Save explicit per-pair preference
note over UI,DB
  Default Off, never inherited from a regular slot.
  Missed-deadline mode is rejected. No patient recording or local reminder control.
end note

== Patient reports an individual intake ==
Patient -> UI: Check PRN medication / bulk check
UI -> Front: Reload today's history and server eligibility
Front -> API: GET /care/history for today
API --> Front: Current counts + active PRN medications
Front --> UI: Fresh state
opt Additional intake for an already checked medication
  UI --> Patient: Confirm displayed count increase
  Patient -> UI: Confirm
  UI -> Front: Reload; verify same date, eligibility and counts
end
UI -> Front: Retain one event UUID + operation UUID per intended intake
loop Each unresolved item (bulk is not atomic)
  Front -> API: PUT report: as_needed:<UUID>, taken, current time, revision
  API -> Care: update_history(...)
  Care -> Care: Check patient scope, account, date, eligibility and revision
  Care -> DB: Check operation receipt / request fingerprint
  alt Successful identical retry
    DB --> Care: Original response; no second record/event
  else Valid new report
    Care -> DB: Save completion report + audit
    opt Today's transition from non-taken to taken
      Care -> DB: queue_as_needed_taken_event(): insert or reuse unique event key
    end
    Care -> DB: Commit report + audit + event + operation receipt atomically
  end
  Care --> API: ACK and any committed outbox ID
  API --> Front: Acknowledge saved report
  Front -> Front: Remove only resolved intention; uncertain retry keeps same IDs
end
note over Front,DB
  New intentional intake = new event UUID. Corrections retain the original UUID.
  Event key = hash(patient, medication, scheduled date, report slot UUID).
  Time/revision edits and uncheck/recheck do not create another event.
  Past reports do not queue new alerts. PRN does not change scheduled progress.
end note

== Durable caregiver push ==
API -> Delivery: Request processing after commit
note over DB,Delivery: Existing outbox worker also recovers/retries due events.
Delivery -> DB: Claim as_needed_dose_completed
Delivery -> DB: Recheck current date, still-taken report, active link,
Delivery -> DB: explicit PRN preference, master switch and push recipients
alt Record no longer current (date passed, undone or deleted)
  Delivery -> DB: Dead letter / AsNeededDoseNoLongerCurrent; do not send
else Valid report
  opt Eligible recipient with token
    Delivery -> Push: caregiver_dose_completed / as_needed / event_key
    Push -> Push: Verify recipient; event-key inbox + foreground identity
    Push --> Caregiver: Individual intake recorded; open linked schedule
  end
  alt Transient delivery failure
    Delivery -> DB: Retry same event; bounded backoff then terminal state
  else No retryable failures
    Delivery -> DB: Mark processed; this is not proof the user saw an alert
  end
end
note over Delivery,Push
  No automatic completion chat, missed deadline or aggregate slot claim.
  Android push tag reuses event_key; distinct intakes remain distinct.
  Repeated display is deduplicated, not guaranteed exactly-once delivery.
end note

== Patient's separate optional local reminder ==
Patient -> UI: Enable PRN check at next selected time
UI -> Front: Save one future booking (default Off)
Front -> Local: Explicit permission + date-specific reminder
Local --> Patient: Neutral check reminder; open schedule only
note over Front,Local
  Patient-scoped preference; no automatic repeat, dose action or snooze.
  Medication master switch and session cleanup cancel the booking.
end note

== Local/demo caregiver monitoring ==
note over UI,Push
  CaregiverNotificationMonitorService reads today's event keys and preferences.
  First snapshot / re-enable establishes a baseline, including alerts-off reports.
  Only newly seen identities notify; previously seen corrections do not replay.
  This fallback does not establish production remote-delivery acceptance.
end note
@enduml
